1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
 Sous-titrage Société Radio-Canada

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
 Sous-titrage Société Radio-Canada

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:29,980
 Sous-titrage Société Radio-Canada

4
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:32,460
 You've already made up your mind and you've already decided how you're going to vote tonight.

5
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:40,640
 I think that's kind of a shame because this is the first time you are really hearing from the population how they feel about this.

6
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:52,440
 And I know you've done door-to-door during your political campaigns, but that is not the same thing as consulting during normal times when people are no longer in a vote.

7
00:01:52,960 --> 00:02:03,400
 So I also noticed that the counselors from Ensemble Morial, you refused the paper copy of the 1,500 signatures or thereabouts that, well, okay.

8
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:12,060
 Okay, well, you originally refused it when it was handed to you by a member of the Cycling Association, and I just want to let you know what is in that, okay.

9
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:27,500
 That is 12 days of citizens going, speaking to people on the street in front of schools, work that you probably should have been doing, and asking them how they felt about the table and bike path, about the changes that you were about to bring.

10
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:34,760
 And we showed them our petition, our little paper, the picture, and we asked them, you know, do you know what's going on?

11
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:36,260
 Do you know how it's going to change?

12
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:40,000
 And the reality is that most people were not aware that you were about to make these changes.

13
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:48,340
 And so for you to be already voting on this when people clearly don't know what it is that you were about to do, I think it's very unfair.

14
00:02:49,640 --> 00:03:00,020
 So that, again, that's almost 1,500 people in the petition, and in Cote de Nege and DG alone, there's 1,128 people.

15
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:06,180
 So, and within one block of the tailbone bike path, there was 464 people.

16
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:07,580
 Now, that's not everybody.

17
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:09,020
 It's only 12 days.

18
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:11,880
 We were going door, we weren't doing the door-to-door.

19
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,920
 We were just standing outside of schools and asking people to sign online.

20
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:26,200
 So I think if you can see that almost 1,500 people are against your changes in just 12 days of asking them their opinions, that maybe you've made up your mind just a little too soon.

21
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:26,840
 Okay.

22
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:31,500
 So before you vote on motion 30-02, I would like you to reconsider.

23
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:34,860
 So is the path perfect?

24
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:35,660
 No.

25
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:38,240
 Are there local residents that don't like it?

26
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:39,900
 Yeah, many of them are here tonight.

27
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:43,820
 But does it make our kids and our bikers safer?

28
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:44,840
 Definitely.

29
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:46,360
 And can it save lives?

30
00:03:46,860 --> 00:03:47,200
 Yes.

31
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:49,240
 And that's not a theoretical thing.

32
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,920
 I have been hit by a car as a pedestrian.

33
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:55,360
 My husband has been hit by a car as a biker.

34
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:59,100
 He ended up with cracked ribs, concussion, scars all over.

35
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:08,900
 My stepson was hit by a car on a bike on Terrebonne right in front of Wellington about five or six years ago.

36
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:10,160
 His bike was totaled.

37
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:12,540
 He was bruised all over, but he is still walking.

38
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:20,200
 So those that think that that's a really safe street because it's really cute and it's got trees and it seems slow, it's still not necessarily safe.

39
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:27,280
 And when you propose to take away that path, well, it's people like my stepson that might end up in a wheelchair for that change.

40
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:41,700
 So what I'd like to ask you, first of all, is before you vote on it, have you communicated to the community what it is that you are really planning to do and what will be coming back in the spring?

41
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:47,040
 So, one, where is the detailed layout of what you're going to change?

42
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:55,440
 So there are areas, like in front of St. Monica's and in front of the road changes at Cavendish, they're not easy to change.

43
00:04:55,860 --> 00:05:09,040
 And when you say you're only taking it off on one side, I want you to think about you're biking along at Cavendish, you hit the red light, now you have to kitty corner to the other side because the traffic changes direction there and you're going to have to be biking on the other side.

44
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:13,700
 Do I want a child crossing diagonally on Cavendish and Tauban?

45
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:14,520
 Obviously not.

46
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:21,840
 So until we actually see your plan, I don't think anybody here can be sure that it is a safe one.

47
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:25,600
 Also, thank you.

48
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:33,540
 And then my second question is, what kind of path will you be bringing back in the spring?

49
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:40,440
 Because you keep talking about a temporary change, but nobody really believes that, okay?

50
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:53,740
 We all know that once you've come and you've scrubbed off all of the yellow lines, you've taken out the bollards and you've put it only on one side and you've put in a new paint line so the cars can park and the signs, when it comes to spring, you're not going to undo all of that.

51
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,940
 You're going to put something else in its place.

52
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:57,680
 What is that something else?

53
00:05:57,680 --> 00:06:03,040
 And before you vote, you should be sharing that information with all of us.

54
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:05,220
 So where is that information, please?

55
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:14,080
 I find it very interesting that you're assuming immediately that what we're saying is incorrect because clearly you don't trust us.

56
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:23,680
 And I totally understand why you would think that we're not trustable because you've clearly positioned yourself on our administration.

57
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:41,000
 I just want to share that in the previous mandate I was elected and the multiple times residents that were not necessarily in favor of the proposed bike path, petitions were deposed with over 1,500 signatures as well.

58
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:47,400
 And those petitions were never considered by the previous administration with regards to the impact that it had on those residents.

59
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:50,840
 We're an administration that is looking at both sides.

60
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:51,820
 And I understand.

61
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:59,460
 Listen, what happened to your stepson, what happened to you, I'm sorry, that's not something that we want in our city.

62
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:01,360
 That's not something that we want in our borough.

63
00:07:01,780 --> 00:07:20,440
 But again, in a spirit of transparency in September, even if there was nothing clear to propose yet or to share, we wanted to alert the residents with regards to the one question that was clearly constantly asked to us with regards to what are you going to do with the Taqban bike path?

64
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:26,140
 The first council that we had, it was an extraordinary council after we were elected in the month of November.

65
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:29,760
 The first question that we had received is, what are you going to do with the bike path?

66
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:31,420
 You've gone door knocking.

67
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,280
 You heard us.

68
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:36,400
 Sunny and myself, we sat in the council in the opposition in the previous mandate.

69
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:42,740
 And all we did was listen to every single council meeting that somebody raised both perspectives.

70
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:51,740
 And I think that we are in this position today with a lot of discontent because the previous administration didn't take the time to listen to both perspectives.

71
00:07:52,480 --> 00:08:03,460
 And I understand that you're going to react that way, but I mean, everybody has a different perspective in this room, whether it's for keeping the bike path on both sides or completely removing it once again.

72
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:15,600
 Again, we're trying to find a middle ground that allows for the infrastructure to stay in place and to eventually add more infrastructure that is clearly needed in the borough of Kodanej and DG.

73
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:21,740
 Again, the proposition is to only remove one side of the bike path for the four months.

74
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,720
 And then after that, it comes back.

75
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:27,460
 And so the both sides will be usable for the rest of the season.

76
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:38,320
 Again, we're waiting for the film or experience to have it ready for deployment in December.

77
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,940
 We don't have that documentation yet.

78
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:52,320
 But we, again, in the spirit of transparency and alerting and communicating with our residents, we're sharing this with you because we want to hear from everybody.

79
00:08:52,320 --> 00:09:06,580
 We want to understand the impact that it will have, and we want to make sure that it responds to the needs of all residents in the borough, including those that have lived over 35 years on Tarbonne,

80
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:14,760
 that have reduced mobility, that don't necessarily have the capacity to walk a few blocks and that need the parking right in front of their home.

81
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:17,140
 There are needs in all of that.

82
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:18,760
 We are an aging population.

83
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:29,320
 More than 30% of our population is at reduced mobility, and we have to be able to consider the needs of all our residents, from young children to our senior population.

84
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:36,500
 There are the HLMs on Tarbonne that clearly had some issues as well with the mise en place of the pièce Tarbonne.

85
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:44,460
 So everybody coming to this council meeting has a very valid perspective and a very valid experience.

86
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:48,860
 In no way are we trying to invalidate all of those experiences.

87
00:09:48,860 --> 00:10:03,180
 What we're trying to do as an administration is find, again, a pathway that is able to respond to the needs of our residents in a way that ensures that we can go forward in the future with additional infrastructure.

88
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:04,220
 Okay.

89
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:11,460
 So you did answer my first question, which is where are the details so that we, the public, that you say are consulting?

90
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:18,240
 I literally, literally just said that our colleagues are working on it with the external firm, and as soon as we have them, they will become public.

91
00:10:18,540 --> 00:10:20,160
 But you're voting before that.

92
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:25,280
 What we're voting on is to transfer, which is exactly what the previous administration did.

93
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:34,940
 So we're voting on, because it's an agglomeration jurisdiction, you have to request from municipal council the ability to put in place the change.

94
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:37,320
 There's a three vote that we're doing.

95
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:39,260
 We're sending it to municipal council.

96
00:10:39,260 --> 00:10:40,820
 It's going to municipal council.

97
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:41,660
 It's going to be voted.

98
00:10:41,660 --> 00:10:48,400
 And once they allow us, that jurisdiction, to put in place the change that we need in our borough, we're going to be able to vote it again in December.

99
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:54,640
 So for multiple times, people are going to be able to come to council and share their perspective and ask us questions.

100
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:55,800
 We respond to them.

101
00:10:55,920 --> 00:11:01,420
 But we've never hidden our intention, and we've always answered the questions of our residents.

102
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:02,120
 Okay.

103
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:10,860
 Well, then I'd like to mention that we have seen your mandate letter to Mr. Teodorescu, which asks him to change the bike path for the entire year.

104
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:18,760
 Mr. Teodorescu is a councillor, so I don't know if your information is correct, but at the same time, you've answered.

105
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:23,940
 I mean, you've gotten your chance to ask your two questions, and so I thank you for your presence tonight.

106
00:11:24,180 --> 00:11:24,920
 Well, don't I get three questions?

107
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:25,980
 No, you don't.

108
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:26,500
 It's two questions.

109
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:29,900
 So you can say something that in the documents that you've shared with us seems to be true?

110
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:33,280
 Every single resident that has shown up to our council meeting has asked two questions.

111
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:37,460
 We've had a few back and forths that are technically not permitted in the Ghejiang town.

112
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,520
 So again, thank you for coming to council.

113
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:41,700
 We're going to pass on to another person.

114
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,320
 Le temps est écoulé, oui, pour la période de questions.

115
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:52,900
 Parfait.

116
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:54,980
 Five minutes a break.

117
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:56,100
 Merci beaucoup.

118
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:06,060
 There's other questions as well about Tara Vaughn, myself and Stephen Jass.

119
00:12:06,340 --> 00:12:06,560
 Okay.

120
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:07,340
 That's it.

121
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:08,660
 That's it.

122
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:13,320
 Il restait deux questions en personne.

123
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:16,280
 On va faire l'extension de 15 minutes, puis on va les laisser.

124
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:17,780
 Pardon?

125
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:19,220
 En présentiel.

126
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:20,000
 Il reste deux questions.

